  "caveats": [
    "A pair whose |delta| is below the noise SD is not known to be a tie — it is known to be unresolvable. Dropping it from training is the right move; dropping it from *evaluation* would be measuring on the easy subset, which is why both the full 360 and the retained subset are reported for every arm.",
    "The BT arms see only 651 pairs (520 per training fold), against 21k rows for lambdarank. A weaker BT number is a sample-size statement, not an architecture one.",
    "Cross-paper pairs (the ligand_cell key) compare out-of-fold scores from two different models with arbitrary relative scale; UP-2b already flags this. It applies to every arm here equally.",
    "The metal graph is a tree on 4 observed nodes, so the additive (hier) model is saturated: u_Ru - u_Rh reproduces the Ru-Rh mean delta exactly. 'Borrowing strength' has no residual degrees of freedom to work with; see UP-18."
  ],
